\section{Compute the Windows Outgoing Area From the Current Stack}

The same argument list can need different stack adjustments
depending on preceding saves. Restrict the calculation to
fixed-prototype Windows x64 calls with scalar arguments that
each occupy at most one eight-byte slot and no stronger
alignment requirement. The input is the current stack-pointer
residue modulo $16$, after all preceding saves, and the number
of already classified stack argument slots. Reserve home space
and the argument slots, then place any padding beyond the last
argument. The stack pointer immediately before the call must
be aligned, and the caller must later restore its old value.

\begin{sudocode}
\Require Current residue $r$, number of stack slots $n$
\Let{H}{32}
\Let{B}{H+8n}
\To{Subtracting this much gives the required residue.}
\Let{p}{(r-B)\bmod 16}
\Let{A}{B+p}
\State Subtract $A$ from the stack pointer
\For{$j\gets 0$ to $n-1$}
  \To{Padding does not shift any argument slot.}
  \State Store argument $j$ at offset $H+8j$
\EndFor
\State Call after placing register arguments
\State Add $A$ to the stack pointer
\end{sudocode}

At entry with residue $8$, a call needing one stack slot
uses $B=40$, padding $0$, and adjustment $40$.
If a prior eight-byte register save changes the residue
to $0$, the same call needs padding $8$ and adjustment
$48$. With the current pointer at \texttt{0x1000}
after the save, subtraction gives \texttt{0x0FD0}.
The stack argument goes at \texttt{0x0FF0}; the
callee sees it at offset $40$ from its entry pointer
\texttt{0x0FC8}. Restoring $48$ after return brings
the pointer back to \texttt{0x1000}, where the previous
save can be handled by the enclosing epilogue.

The invariant is that the adjusted pointer is aligned and
the argument offsets are fixed independently of padding.
For $n=0$, home space is still $32$ bytes. A production
prologue must also account for existing outgoing areas,
unwind rules, frame size, and stack probing where required.
This arithmetic does not establish callee-save register
preservation or assign aggregate arguments. Test those
contracts separately from the stack residues.

\section{Verify at the Call Boundary}

A thunk's preservation obligation comes from its incoming convention, even if its outgoing call uses a different preserved set. For example, a Windows-facing thunk calling a System V routine cannot expect that routine to preserve \texttt{rdi}, \texttt{rsi}, or the low 128 bits of \texttt{xmm6} through \texttt{xmm15}. Generate the enclosing platform's unwind information for the actual saves and stack adjustment. Test both call directions against independently compiled callees that return a checksum of distinct sentinels, clobber permitted volatile registers, and verify preserved registers and stack restoration. The dossier's \href{https://github.com/Chubek/TheTomeOfLangDev/blob/HEAD/dossier-on-modern-cc-design/chapters/42-adaptive-abi-negotiation.md}{Adaptive ABI Negotiation} considers where such adapters fit in a negotiated interface.
